findings.description:
Constructor names and order are identical for Instr_ok (73), Instrs_ok (5), Expr_ok (1), Instr_ok2 (6), Instrs_ok2 (5), Expr_ok2 (1), Step_pure (54), Step_read (47) and Step (23). The only name differences are Rocq's reserved-word prefixes (res_if, res_return, res_seq, Rel__x).

Premise fingerprints (premise count and counts of Forall, Forall2, ranges, lengths, lookups, ≠none, wf_, comparisons and connectives) are identical for every constructor of all 346 inductives common to both files. The only exceptions are these Rocq-to-Lean renderings, each checked equivalent:
- `holds_upto P n` (= Forall P (iotaN 0 n)) ↔ `Forall P (List.range n)`;
- `List_Foralli` ↔ `Forall₂ _ (List.range n) l` with n = |l|;
- `mkseqN` ↔ `List.range n |>.map`;
- `list_slice` ↔ take/drop;
- `list_update_func` ↔ `List.modify`;
- `list_repeat` ↔ `List.replicate`;
- the Q→N coercion (Z.to_N ∘ Qfloor) ↔ `rat_to_nat` (equal for every sign);
- `lookup_total`/`!` ↔ `[i]!`/`Option.get!`.

The defaults used by `[i]!` and `Option.get!` are reached only out of range or on none, and every rule lookup is guarded by a bound or `≠ none` premise or by typing. Lean's `List.contains` stands in for Rocq's `\in`; on the preservation path it is only used over types that derive LawfulBEq (num_, uN/vec_, lane_, externaddr, name), so it is equivalent to membership. Context append is identical: Lean's `Option.orElse` matches Rocq's left-biased `option_append`. The accessors, `default_`, `fun_blocktype` and `size` are identical. Step_read_is_wf and Step_is_wf have the same statements as Rocq's hand-edited versions, which are Rocq's only definition-level hand-edits. The top-level t_preservation is identical in Lean, Rocq and Isabelle (fixed ts).

Re-checked and confirmed as meaning-preserving:
- the hlen premises of wf_tableinsts_preserves and wf_memoryinsts_preserves;
- mem_store_extension's len : Q -> Nat. This is equivalent because both versions pin len to |b_lst|, and Rocq's list_slice_update takes j : N. The Lean list_slice_update (HelperLemmas l.159) has the same structural recursion as Rocq's (wasm.v:66);
- t_read_preservation's Vals_ok;
- store_extension_reduce proved without Step_is_wf.
That last proof is still not sorry-free. Through store_extension_reduce_aux it uses nbytes__is_wf, ibytes__is_wf, wrap___is_wf and vbytes__is_wf, all among the 32 known numeric sorries. This is recorded in for-claude/is_wf_theorems.md l.75 but not in the theorem's doc comment, which mentions only Step_is_wf. Also num_default_is_well_formed is a Lean-only proof of a lemma that Rocq has commented out; the TP header l.24 documents this.
